      "passage": null,
      "classification": "disputed",
      "reasoning": "2 Maccabees narrates his death (ch. 9) before the cleansing (10:1–8) and closes the section \"such were the events of the end of Antiochus\" (10:9); its letters of year 148 include one in which Antiochus V speaks of his father as dead (11:23). 1 Maccabees (6:1–16) and Josephus (Ant. 12.9.1) have him die in Persia after hearing that the Jews had pulled down the abomination. The Babylonian king list reports news of his death in Kislimu 148 SE (Babylonian reckoning) — the same month-name as the rededication (25 Chislev 148): if 1 Maccabees used the spring (Babylonian) epoch the two events fall within weeks of each other (Dec 164); on the autumn epoch the rededication (Dec 165) precedes the death by a year. 2 Maccabees' arrangement is often thought thematic, but that was not verified here. Unresolved.",
